## 3. MCP Tool Instructions

When the `cybermp` MCP server is active in Cursor, invoke these tools before guessing signatures:
- `cybermp_get_event`: Look up verified event listener signatures, payloads, and execution contexts (e.g. `playerConnected`, `damage`).
- `cybermp_get_type`: Look up TypeScript interface definitions and properties (e.g. `MpPlayer`, `MpVehicle`, `Vector3`).
- `cybermp_get_rpc_flow`: Generate paired sender/receiver code snippets across contexts.
- `cybermp_search_docs`: Search official guides, runbooks, and architectural patterns.
- `cybermp_lookup_tweakdb`: Look up verified Cyberpunk 2077 TweakDB record IDs for status effects, armed vehicles, weapons, and workspots.

## 4. TypeScript Setup & Imports

- Install packages: `@cybermp/server-types`, `@cybermp/client-types`, `@cybermp/browser-types`.
- `events` and `commands` are global runtime objects provided by CyberMP. Do not import `events` as a value from `@cybermp/*`. Only import types:
  ```typescript
  import type { MpPlayer } from '@cybermp/server-types';
  ```
- Keep separate `tsconfig.server.json` and `tsconfig.client.json` to avoid context collision.

## 5. Resource Architecture & Configuration

In CyberMP, resources reside in the server's `resources/` folder. Every resource MUST contain a `resource.toml` manifest, and be listed in the root `server.toml`:

```toml
# server.toml (in server root)
resources = ["my-resource"]
```

```toml
# resources/my-resource/resource.toml
#:schema https://schemas.cyber.mp/resource/schema.json

server_script = ["./server.js"]
client_script = ["./client.js"]
file = ["./browser/**/*"]
cef_url = "./browser/index.html"
use_game_natives = true
hotreload = true
```

Folder layout:
```
resources/my-resource/
├── resource.toml           # Official manifest (REQUIRED)
├── server.js               # Node.js server script
├── client.js               # V8 in-game client script
└── browser/                # CEF Web UI files (HTML/CSS/JS)
    └── index.html
```
